# Pairs with AtomicOnOwner. The naive fix for #4474: a saga bound to the resized
# copy R, whose resize is undone after the swap, has terminals R refuses once
# the undo discarded it; following that refusal to the copy the tree resolves to
# re-sends the shard's terminal, with its committed-values backstop, to the old
# copy, which the undo made the tree again and which lays keys out by the same
# map. Terminals R took before the discard are discarded with R, so the old copy
# gets the batch on some shards only. Production today stalls instead
# (SagaCompletesDiscardedCopyRefusesTerminal); this mutation stands against a
# fix that follows the refusal.
MODULE: AtomicOnOwnerDiscardedCopyTerminalRedirects
TARGET: AtomicOnOwner
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: terminals of a saga bound to an undone resized copy are re-sent to the old copy, landing part of the batch there
PERTURBS: SagaTerminal

--- FIND
           hit == IF bound = R /\ ~Live(R) THEN {}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a terminal R's redirect refuses is re-sent to the old copy.
           hit == IF bound = R /\ ~Live(R) THEN {<<T, s>>}
--- END
